2. Cross-check output: the summary line is the last non-empty line of stdout. A problem line (starts with SC- or SL-) may go to stdout or to stderr.
3. X8 (Q24): the function receives a week as an object that is not a valid week ({ meta: { level: 2, week: 5 } }) in the position of w05. It must not throw. It gives exactly one problem line that starts with "w05: ". The 5 list rows of that week add no other problem. rows stays 44. (Q23 fixes the argument type StorytimeWeek[], so the function must accept a bad entry and report it.)
4. X7 (Q24): the problem text is exactly "SC-w02-d3: the week file has no share".
5. A row with a wrong cell count gives one problem of its id and no second "missing row" problem. The rows count includes it. A repeated row id gives one problem of that id. An extra row gives one problem of its id.
6. Teacher book HTML: the icon element (attribute data-share-media) sits inside the div class st-step of the shot step. The block is found by the id in the title ("<id> · "), so the title text must not change. The D5 block holds the caption of day 4 (it prints in the recall group of day 5). The D6 block holds the caption of day 5 (it prints in the opening of day 5).
7. T10: the share option adds only the icon, the label, the caption, the consent line, and the length line to the visible text. An extra heading fails T10.
8. T5 and T9 count the consent line in the visible text, after tags, style, script, and svg are removed and entities are decoded. The consent line and the length line sit in the block of the first shot of the first day that has a share (A3 in w01 and w02, A2 in w08, B5 when day 1 has no share).
9. The icon is an inline svg (the element itself, or inside the element with the attribute). It holds only the colours #000, #000000, black, none, or currentColor.
10. T4 counts a label in a block as the count in the share-on block (after the removal of the captions, the consent line, and the length line) minus the count in the share-off block. It needs exactly 1 for the label of the media and 0 for the other label.
11. Both scripts: the source holds the text "a === '--share'". The compile call passes share (shorthand or property). Every renderChromePdf call passes an argument named share. The usage text of both scripts names --share (the print usage also names --loops, as now). A lone --share is accepted: the exit code is 2 (a missing source or level) and stderr holds no "unknown argument". An unknown flag still exits 2 and stderr names the flag.
12. The script path is dashboard/scripts/storytime/check-share-captions.ts. The tests load it with a path variable. It must export shareCaptionProblems(weeks, labels, list) and run main only when it is the entry point (the pattern of check-weeks.ts).

